nt type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.anthropic.com/research\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 58\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content cite1†Skip to footer L1: \nL2:   * Research\nL3:   * cite2†Policy L4:   * Commitments\nL5:   * Learn\nL6:   * cite3†News L7: \nL8: cite4†Try Claude†claude.ai L9: \nL10: # Research\nL11: \nL12: Our research teams investigate the safety, inner workings, and societal impacts of AI models—so that artificial intelligence has a positive impact as it becomes increasingly capable.\nL13: \nL14: Research teams:cite5†Alignment cite6†Economics cite7†Interpretability cite8†Societal Impacts cite9†Frontier Red Team L15: ### Alignment\nL16: \nL17: The Alignment team works to understand the risks of AI models and develop ways to ensure that future ones remain helpful, honest, and harmless.\nL18: \nL19: ### Economics\nL20: \nL21: The Economics team studies how AI is reshaping the economy, including work, productivity, and economic opportunity.\nL22: \nL23: ### Frontier Red Team\nL24: \nL25: The Frontier Red Team analyzes the implications of frontier AI models for cybersecurity, biosecurity, and autonomous systems.\nL26: ### Interpretability\nL27: \nL28: The mission of the Interpretability team is to understand how large language models work internally, as a foundation for AI safety and positive outcomes.\nL29: ### Societal Impacts\nL30: \nL31: Working closely with the Anthropic Policy and Safeguards teams, Societal Impacts is a technical research team that explores how AI is used in the real world.\nL32: \nL33: cite10†Image: Scenarios for our Economic Future L34: cite11†Scenarios for our Economic Future Anthropic’s Economics team is sharing a new model of how AI may affect economic growth, jobs, wages, and more by 2030. The model lets you explore the scenarios, tell us what you think will happen, and see how your answers compare to +10,000 Americans. L35: cite12†ScienceSep 23, 2026 Claude discovers a novel enzyme system with CRISPR-like repeats We’re announcing a new life sciences research group and laboratory at Anthropic.\nL36: This post introduces the team behind this work and shares early results in which Claude discovered a novel enzyme system with properties reminiscent of CRISPR, with only high-level direction from our scientists. cite13†Sep 17, 2026 Measurements for understanding the pace of AI development inside frontier labs Today, the world can’t see what’s going on inside AI labs.\nL37: Anthropic is proposing new metrics that would give the public visibility into frontier AI development. cite14†ScienceSep 4, 2026 Formalizing Fermat's Last Theorem We are sharing the first complete computer-checked proof of Fermat’s Last Theorem.\nL38: Claude worked largely autonomously over 11 days to write the proof in the Lean programming language. cite15†AlignmentSep 9, 2026 An alignment assessment of recent cybersecurity incidents We present an alignment assessment of four incidents in which Claude models gained unauthorized access to real third-party systems. L39: ## Publications\nL40: \nL41: Search[Input: Search]\nL42: \nL43: Date Category Title\nL44:   * cite16†Oct 1, 2026Science Claude-shaped science L45:   * cite17†Sep 30, 2026Economics What work can robots do? L46:   * cite18†Sep 29, 2026Societal Impacts What do you want from AI? L47:   * cite19†Sep 29, 2026Frontier Red Team GLM-5.3 and the spread of advanced cyber capabilities L48:   * cite20†Sep 25, 2026Science Yes, Claude can do Nine Loops L49:   * cite21†Sep 24, 2026Economics Project Swap: What happens when agents trade for us? L50:   * cite22†Sep 17, 2026Science How Claude is uplifting biomolecular modeling L51:   * cite23†Sep 10, 2026Frontier Red Team Measuring tactical intelligence targeting and conventional weapons capabilities of AI models L52:   * cite15†Sep 9, 2026Alignment An alignment assessment of recent cybersecurity incidents L53:   * cite14†Sep 4, 20